WEBVTT

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:02.625
Every contact sticker makes the same trade.

00:00:02.731 --> 00:00:04.758
Print your number, and it's public forever.

00:00:04.864 --> 00:00:07.290
Leave it off, and no one can reach you when it matters.

00:00:08.223 --> 00:00:11.146
PassQR Tag carries a code, and nothing else.

00:00:11.295 --> 00:00:14.005
Someone scans it and writes, right in their browser.

00:00:14.111 --> 00:00:14.773
No app.

00:00:14.794 --> 00:00:15.584
No account.

00:00:15.647 --> 00:00:16.865
No numbers exchanged.

00:00:17.852 --> 00:00:19.751
Anyone can photograph a QR code.

00:00:19.814 --> 00:00:21.351
Not everyone is standing at it.

00:00:21.478 --> 00:00:23.271
The relay checks they're really there,

00:00:23.313 --> 00:00:24.423
before it interrupts you.

00:00:25.401 --> 00:00:27.300
When it's urgent, it escalates.

00:00:27.406 --> 00:00:30.095
Your wallet pass, your phone, a text,

00:00:30.222 --> 00:00:33.240
then your second contact, and it stops the moment you reply.

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:36.492
Be reachable, without publishing your number.

00:00:36.662 --> 00:00:38.070
PassQR Tag.

00:00:38.112 --> 00:00:41.908
Ask for a tag, at tag.passqr.com.
